# NeMo Guardrails - Colang 2.x Entry Point
#
# We do NOT import llm, guardrails, or core because the installed NeMo
# version's standard library files contain Colang 2.x syntax that the
# lark parser rejects (UnexpectedToken at import statements).
#
# We therefore define flow main directly here with no imports and WITHOUT
# the `@override` decorator. `@override` requires a pre-existing base flow
# with the same name to override (Colang 2.x hard-errors at LLMRails
# construction time with "Override flow with name 'main' does not override
# any flow with that name!" otherwise) — since no library flow named `main`
# is ever imported here, there is nothing to override.
#
# BUG HISTORY (2026-08-02): This `@override` bug was previously masked by an
# unrelated Colang syntax error in generated_stpa_rails.co (lowercase `true`
# instead of `True`) that caused RailsConfig.from_path() to fail first,
# triggering the transparent-fallback path below `@override` was fixed. Once
# that syntax bug was fixed, LLMRails construction proceeded far enough to
# reach — and fail on — this `@override` defect. Both bugs independently
# disabled all NeMo semantic rails; both must be fixed together.
#
# The Python validate_with_nemo() has a "No main flow" pass-through guard
# so NeMo config failures are non-fatal; OPA + STPA remain authoritative.

flow main
  match UtteranceUser() as $msg
  await bot say $msg.text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# self check input — locally-defined replacement for NeMo's library flow
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NeMo's built-in `nemoguardrails.library.self_check.input_check` flow (which
# config.yml's deprecated `rails.input.flows: [self check input]` normally
# resolves against) cannot be imported here — the installed NeMo version's
# library Colang 2.x files fail to parse (see header comment above). We
# therefore define our own `flow self check input` locally, using the same
# flow name NeMo's rails-flow-generation code expects (see
# nemoguardrails/rails/llm/config.py::_generate_rails_flows(), which emits
# `flow input rails $input_text` containing an indented call to this exact
# flow name), but backed by our own CustomSelfCheckInputAction instead of
# NeMo's library SelfCheckInputAction + self_check_input prompt template.
flow self check input
  $allowed = await CustomSelfCheckInputAction
  if not $allowed
    bot refuse to respond
    abort
